Use **`INDEX`**. It returns the row at an absolute position along the axis (`ROWS`, `COLUMNS`, `ROWS COLUMNS`, or `COLUMNS ROWS`). Because it returns a row and not a scalar, wrap it in `CALCULATE`:

```dax
// Value at the 3rd position on the rows axis
Third Value = CALCULATE ( [Sales Amount], INDEX ( 3, ROWS ) )

// Negative positions count from the end: -1 = last
Last Value = CALCULATE ( [Sales Amount], INDEX ( -1, ROWS ) )

// Restart the position count within each group (e.g., per Year in a Year > Month hierarchy)
First In Group = CALCULATE ( [Sales Amount], INDEX ( 1, ROWS, HIGHESTPARENT ) )
```

For the first or last position specifically, the visual-calc shortcuts `FIRST([Sales Amount])` and `LAST([Sales Amount])` do the same thing more concisely. Use `INDEX` for any other fixed position.
